WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.702
-I love it
when you guys are here.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.637
Is this the first time you guys
have actually been on the show?

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.773
-No, we're always here.
They're always here.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.240
-We're Robert's cheer squad.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.877
-We love supporting Robert.
We love your show.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.912
And I love the cheese wheel
in the green room

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.780
every time we come here.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.182
It's awesome.
-Yeah. You do. Thank you, yeah.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.852
-Actually, tomorrow
marks the second year

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.553
that Robert's been coming
on your show.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.855
How exciting is that?
-Thank you, buddy.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:25.324
♪♪

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.660
-And when he first came
on your show --

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.496
I actually posted a picture
of Robert and Dad

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.732
side-by-side
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.901
I think you have the photo.
They're both holding a snake.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.804
And it brought tears to my eyes.
It was so special.

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:40.473
Isn't that just amazing?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.209
And Robert is more and more
like Dad every single day,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.477
and we're so proud of him.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.811
-And you're not at all like Jay.

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:47.680
-Yeah, I'm a little more scared
than Jay was, yeah.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.382
-Maybe their expression
is slightly different.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.417
-A little more frightened.
-We're very proud of you, too.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.018
You've done so well
with all the animals.

00:00:53.018 --> 00:00:55.588
-You guys are just
great for what you do.
I want to get into this.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.624
Tell us about Wildlife Warriors.
What is it?

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:01.794
-Yeah, well, Wildlife Warriors,
it was started many years ago.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.597
17 years ago, actually.
Mom and Dad first started it.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.534
As a way to unite everyone

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.868
to stand up for those
that don't have a voice.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.737
So it covers humanitarian

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:14.006
and wildlife issues
all over the world.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:17.576
And since it's started, they
vowed to put every cent back in.

00:01:17.576 --> 00:01:19.245
So whenever people donate,

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.748
everything that we make
goes straight back into there.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.150
And it's protecting animals
all over the world,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.152
and it's giving people
the chance

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.920
to really have a voice,
have their say.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.658
In Australia, crocs have
now been really on the decline.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:34.227
Their eggs are being taken

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.929
and harvested
to be turned into meat.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.664
So we're really working hard

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:41.601
to really change the society's
perspective on conservation.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.603
'Cause, ultimately,
it's about us, as well.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.004
-Yeah. That's good for you.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.839
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:48.407
That's great.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:52.779
But, also, the animal hospital
part of the Australia Zoo

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.547
and what you do --

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.582
How many animals
have you treated?

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.852
-Over 82,000 animals.
-82,000.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.788
-82,000. Yeah.
So, we opened in 2004.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.190
And we rescue sick,
injured, orphaned animals

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.392
just to get them
back out into the wild.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.527
And it's so special.
It's what we love.

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.830
-That's amazing.
And the money from the zoo,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.166
some profits from there
go to the hospital?

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.900
-Yeah. Completely.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.036
It's really exciting
when you visit Australia Zoo.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.738
It's all about the wildlife.
It's hands on with everything.

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.775
And if you're walking with
a tiger or hugging a koala

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.210
or feeding a giraffe,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.747
those experiences fund
all of the nonprofit activities

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.415
that we have around the world.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.217
So it's really awesome.
Come to Australia Zoo.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.052
You can go to
WildlifeWarriors.org

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.320
and sign the petition
to protect crocodiles.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.789
And it's very special.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.625
-You have some big news
about a giraffe.

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:42.595
-Oh, yeah.
-Yes. We do.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:46.465
At Australia Zoo, we actually
have some very exciting news.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.534
One of our giraffes is pregnant

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.670
and is going to be
giving birth very soon.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.105
We're so excited.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:56.442
And we wanted to give you the
chance to name this little baby.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.612
I know you've selected
a couple names, and --

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.681
-I'm excited. Two names.
-Two names.

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:05.117
And then we'll let
all of you guys choose

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:08.120
which one's the best, and --
Yeah, it's coming very --

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.688
-Do we know if it's
a boy or girl?

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:11.190
-Not at this point.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.727
You know, giraffes --
it's 15 months, the gestation

00:03:15.727 --> 00:03:18.431
So it takes a long time
before that little one pops out.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.833
So it's pretty amazing.
-I'm excited.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.436
Thank you for giving me
this opportunity.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.671
And thank you
for coming on the show.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.174
And thank you for everything
you're doing for animals

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.842
around the world and everything.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.078
We love you, guys, so much.
-We love you.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.980
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.982
-Thank you so much.
-Terri, Bindi, and Robert Irwin.

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:39.351
Visit WildlifeWarriors.org

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:41.421
for details on
how to get involved.

